{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sharing the Housework"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Finally, A Clean Home"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Placeholder"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Placeholder"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": ""}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Causative - <span class=\"italic\">get</span>/<span class=\"italic\">have</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use a causative verb when you want to talk about something that someone else did for you or for another person. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the causative verbs <span class=\"italic\">get</span>/<span class=\"italic\">have </span>when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br /><span class=\"italic\">Have your spouse or housemates clean up after themselves. </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this sentence <span class=\"italic\">you </span>ask or persuade your spouse to clean up after themselves."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the causative is: <br /><br /> Subject + <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + object + verb <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Have someone remind</span> everyone.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "or"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">get</span> + object + infinitive  <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Get everyone to choose</span> their favorite music to play.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, you use <span class=\"italic\">get</span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have everyone decide together what to clean. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Get everyone to choose their favorite music to play, and order pizza for lunch. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Maybe after this you won't have to get everyone to do it again."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have your spouse or housemates clean up after themselves. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have someone remind everyone."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Explaining How Things Were Done"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "  You use <span class=\"italic\">be supposed to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">was going</span> to to explain how things were done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to </span>when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements. You can use this structure using the Past tense to talk about things that you were obligated to do, but didn't or couldn't do. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is: <br /><br /> Subject + To be +<span class=\"italic\"> supposed to</span> + verb <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">Another thing <span class=\"strong\">we were all supposed to be doing</span> to help the environment was not litter. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br /> When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together.  <br /><br /> Like this: Be suppose_to"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the structure<span class=\"strong\"> was going to </span> when you want to talk about things that you had planned or intended to do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is:<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">was</span>/<span class=\"italic\">were </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">going to</span> + verb <br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">were going to spend</span> less time driving and more time walking.  </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We were supposed to recycle. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You were supposed to take all of your recyclables out of the weekly trash, too! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Obviously we have not been doing what we were supposed to be doing or there wouldn't be a crisis!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You were going to spend less time driving and more time walking."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le07ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to recommend"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "To give an advice "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I recommend dividing the chores equally."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you need to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spouse "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "husband or wife"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:Have your spouse or housemates clean up after themselves. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overwhelming "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very large"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You do not want the housework to become overwhelming again do you?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "properly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "most suitable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Schedule a major cleaning day into your calendar when everyone is supposed to help out and do it properly. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to help out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to provide what is necessary to accomplish a task"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everyone is supposed to help out and do it properly. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tedious "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " long and tiresome"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:Isn't it better to make things fun rather than tedious?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "entertaining "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "fun, amusing "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  You could make it entertaining."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to maintain"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to keep "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Here are some ways you can maintain a clean house."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob11aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "You and two of your friends are moving into a house together."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The place needs to be cleaned so you have decided to invite people over to help you with your cleaning day."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm a list of things that need to be done then write up a fun \u2018asking for your help' invitation to other friends."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use clarification questions to encourage agreement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Offer food and music as incentives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Bring your invitation to class and show a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write an invitation to have people help me clean up my new house or apartment. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for help."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use clarification questions to encourage agreement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I offer food and music as incentives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my invitation with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain how to do things in a spoken way. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about solving problems."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can ask for clarification and encourage agreement. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How often do people in your circle of friends and family  work together to get things done quickly?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How often is this type of thing done for your community - at a community center or church?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], 